<p>Here we are adding an event listener to the <code>guessSubmit</code> but=
ton. This is a method that takes two input values (called <em>arguments</em=
>) =E2=80=94 the type of event we are listening out for (in this case <code=
>click</code>) as a string, and the function we want to run when the event =
occurs (in this case, <code>checkGuess()</code>). Note that we don't need t=
o specify the parentheses when writing it inside <a href=3D"https://develop=
er.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/EventTarget/addEventListener" title=3D"ad=
dEventListener()"><code>addEventListener()</code></a>.</p>
<p>Try saving and refreshing your code now, and your example should work =
=E2=80=94 to a point. The only problem now is that if you guess the correct=
 answer or run out of guesses, the game will break because we've not yet de=
fined the <code>setGameOver()</code> function that is supposed to be run on=
ce the game is over. Let's add our missing code now and complete the exampl=
e functionality.</p>
